    "title": "Veterinary drug supplier to pay $100K for failing to flag Putnam vet's suspicious orders - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By ANTHONY DAMCOTT ,\n6 hours ago PUTNAM COUNTY, W.Va. (WCHS) — A global veterinary drug distributor has agreed to a settlement for allegations that it didn't identify large oxycodone HCL orders from a Putnam County veterinarian as suspicious, prosecutors said. MWI, also known as MWI Animal Health, agreed on Wednesday to pay $100,000 to resolve... Read full article",
